onal wave, would move this rating.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Open seat: Neal Dunn (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Florida's 2nd District, anchored in the Panhandle and Tallahassee outskirts, leans Republican by about eight points, and Neal Dunn's retirement leaves the seat open rather than vulnerable. Austin Rogers won a contested Republican primary in August and enters the general election with a decisive financial edge, roughly $1.0 million raised and about $1.4 million in outside support, against about $348,000 raised and $28,000 on hand for Democrat Amanda Green. National analysts overwhelmingly rate the seat Solid or Safe Republican, with a minority calling it Likely or Lean Republican, and prediction markets give Green roughly a one-in-ten chance.\n\nNo credible public polls test the general-election matchup, so expectations rest on the district's partisan lean, the money gap, and expert consensus. A national environment that has favored Democrats this cycle offers Green some hope, but she would need a substantial shift to put this open seat in play.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0837, "margin": -8.48}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.084, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1162, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.1045, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0789, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0848, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.1006, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0806, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0753, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0679, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0619, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0853, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0683, "margin": -10.5}]}